-9830-51162d55cab8" :answer-field/choices "answer-9756f17c-547d-5717-b4bf-797326722482"] ["answer-field-105a3af8-27bf-5111-9830-51162d55cab8" :answer-field/choices "answer-e1618446-0931-52ac-b916-219dfe148992"] ["answer-field-105a3af8-27bf-5111-9830-51162d55cab8" :answer-field/choices "answer-097cd6bb-a98e-56ad-9b47-98d16bfbaa02"] ["answer-field-105a3af8-27bf-5111-9830-51162d55cab8" :answer-field/choices "answer-cbb420df-0b0d-5edc-867c-19a182ed465c"] ["question-a946e21d-5a37-5585-a234-01e6acc34eca" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-105a3af8-27bf-5111-9830-51162d55cab8"] [17592186192681 :knowledge-point/questions "question-a946e21d-5a37-5585-a234-01e6acc34eca"] ["question-acbab80b-b003-5343-8102-3dfe5d2664d2" :question/id #uuid "acbab80b-b003-5343-8102-3dfe5d2664d2"] ["question-acbab80b-b003-5343-8102-3dfe5d2664d2" :question/math-academy-id "q-138532"] ["question-acbab80b-b003-5343-8102-3dfe5d2664d2" :question/problem "The covariance matrix $C$ of some particular observations is shown below. \n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the third principal component of the data, given that the eigenvalues of $C$ are $8,$ $5,$ and $2.$"] ["question-acbab80b-b003-5343-8102-3dfe5d2664d2" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the unit eigenvectors of the covariance matrix $C$ are called the principal components of the data. If \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}>{\\lambda }_{2}>⋯>{\\lambda }_{n}\n$$\n\nare the eigenvalues of $C$ written in descending order, then: \n\n- the $1$st principal component is the unit eigenvector ${u}_{1}$ corresponding to the $1$st eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{1},$\n\n- the $2$nd principal component is the unit eigenvector ${u}_{2}$ corresponding to the $2$nd eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{2},$\n\n- $⋯$\n\nand so on.\n\nIn our case, the eigenvalues of the covariance matrix $C,$ in descending order, are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=8,\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=5,\\,{\\lambda }_{3}=2.\n$$\n\nSo, we need the unit eigenvector that corresponds to the eigenvalue ${\\lambda }_{3}=2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C-2I & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]-2[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $(C-2I)x=0$ gives the eigenvector ${v}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nFinally, dividing ${v}_{3}$ by its norm $‖{v}_{3}‖=3,$ we get \n\n$$\n{u}_{3}=\\frac{{v}_{3}}{‖{v}_{3}‖}=\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$"] ["question-acbab80b-b003-5343-8102-3dfe5d2664d2" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] ["answer-field-0b6d3086-6051-52d2-aff8-a787552ec9a0" :answer-field/id #uuid "0b6d3086-6051-52d2-aff8-a787552ec9a0"] ["answer-f878ea67-ef32-52af-ab6f-9dbc92982da8" :answer/id #uuid "f878ea67-ef32-52af-ab6f-9dbc92982da8"] ["answer-f878ea67-ef32-52af-ab6f-9dbc92982da8" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-f878ea67-ef32-52af-ab6f-9dbc92982da8" :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-c7f8f5f8-4566-550b-af9b-f5286609b0bd" :answer/id #uuid "c7f8f5f8-4566-550b-af9b-f5286609b0bd"] ["answer-c7f8f5f8-4566-550b-af9b-f5286609b0bd" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-c7f8f5f8-4566-550b-af9b-f5286609b0bd" :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-cff31548-be96-50f5-b36c-0864299f187b" :answer/id #uuid "cff31548-be96-50f5-b36c-0864299f187b"] ["answer-cff31548-be96-50f5-b36c-0864299f187b" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-cff31548-be96-50f5-b36c-0864299f187b" :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]"] ["answer-d77ccd62-a3e0-5ccb-86f5-b0e37d719ee6" :answer/id #uuid "d77ccd62-a3e0-5ccb-86f5-b0e37d719ee6"] ["answer-d77ccd62-a3e0-5ccb-86f5-b0e37d719ee6" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-d77ccd62-a3e0-5ccb-86f5-b0e37d719ee6" :answer/v